{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$f : M \\to N$", "MATH_0003": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0004": "$P \\in \\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0005": "$f \\otimes 1_P: M \\otimes_R P \\to N \\otimes_R P$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-universally-injective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f7a7db0ab1b8a2e5e3b04322eb380978c26260d29a1909d6cca05aa51e90fbcc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6f592303cc0461e20eb2a126de133dae48ab381481f7b3b8e31974dae18108fc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a ring. Recall that a morphism <MATH_0002> in <MATH_0003>\nis <TEXTITOPEN_0001>universally injective<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for all <MATH_0004>,\nthe morphism <MATH_0005> is injective.\nSee Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c4f4f9750dd5969b563076dcff6c4e89808993253df8fb46479f8a1fd4f253c0", "unit_id": "tag:08WJ:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f: R \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-universally-injective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a69b4113b30344ae0ab2dd2d54cdc3130a171464491f7914233fd34c8f3716f9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:43f08114949739edc5acd7b5d4a592e519f2a06fce1f60e9e693c3974698689e", "source_text": "A ring map <MATH_0001> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>universally injective<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif it is universally injective as a morphism in <MATH_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d030a96d0e534cfdd72e164161de0f50dde0151fd84a6efc22c1b84341b07063", "unit_id": "tag:08WL:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{Rings}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-split-injection-universally-injective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:95ca3ca0a1ba030d7e7272d0581b4b34dbed6b917add9bf2cd4b972564bddf62", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ba96711e09186c7f52ebdd0b99d5ec0fbd7e9034f97f29228212e1af3fa73170", "source_text": "Any split injection in <MATH_0001> is universally injective. In particular,\nany split injection in <MATH_0002> is universally injective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:64cc9b5e0bae5b5acfb55d7bd58b25b3f70ab3b60ee30250ebb37bb396b1037d", "unit_id": "tag:08WM:statement"}
